// A prefab: a piece of a place, drawn as rows of glyphs, and what each glyph
// stands for; see `treasure_room.ron` for the full field list.
//
// Part 3's captives, shackled under guard; freed, they follow: 'C' is a
// `Mark`, read by `src/vaults.rs`'s own `spawn_chained_captive`, which
// shackles the monster it stands there exactly as `population.rs`'s own
// captive is shackled. One cell: the guard over it is a flavor that
// risks a monster slot's own distance-from-entry and lair-band checks
// for no mechanism of its own, so it stays scenery, the shackles beside
// an empty post.
(
    name: "Captives in Chains",
    ground: "hall floor",
    rows: [
        "s.s",
        ".C.",
    ],
    legend: {
        '.': Tile("hall floor"),
        's': Prop("shackles"),
        'C': Mark,
    },
)
